{"term":"rash","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:615a42146732b3e2a2","definition":"Acting too quickly without considering the consequences and risks; not careful; hasty.","example":"rash words spoken in the heat of debate","pos":"adj","synonyms":["foolhardy","heady","impulsive","precipitate","daring","devil-may-care","headstrong","heedless","impetuous","imprudent","impulsive","precipitant","precipitate","precipitous","quick-and-dirty","rash","reckless","sudden","temeritous"],"antonyms":["prudent","unrash","shy","timid","cautious","careful"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["overrash","rashful","rashling","rashly","rashness","unrash"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rash#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:35c6836eb1a98f5f34","definition":"Of corn or other grains: so dry as to fall out of the ear with handling.","example":"","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Northern-England, archaic","register":"Northern-England, archaic","wordFamily":["overrash","rashful","rashling","rashly","rashness","unrash"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rash#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:646cb55f1c85e49a28","definition":"Requiring swift action; pressing; urgent.","example":"My Lord, I ſcarce haue leiſure to ſalute you, / My matter is ſo raſh: […]","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete, rare","register":"obsolete, rare","wordFamily":["overrash","rashful","rashling","rashly","rashness","unrash"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rash#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9984640f14ad1d292d","definition":"Taking effect quickly and strongly; fast-acting.","example":"[T]he vnited veſſel of their bloud, / […] / Shall neuer leake, though it doe vvorke as ſtrong, / As Aconitum, or raſh gunpovvder.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete, rare","register":"obsolete, rare","wordFamily":["overrash","rashful","rashling","rashly","rashness","unrash"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rash#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c102b5dcd473c09d63","definition":"Synonym of rashly (“in a rash manner; hastily or without due consideration”).","example":"Soft Gooddie Sheepe (then ſaid the Foxe) not ſoe: / Vnto the King ſo raſh ye may not goe, / He is vvith greater matter buſied, / Than a Lambe, or the Lambes ovvne mothers hed.","pos":"adv","synonyms":["rashly"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic","wordFamily":["overrash","rashful","rashling","rashly","rashness","unrash"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rash#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2ecd5d6de1f77dab66","definition":"An area of inflamed and irritated skin characterized by reddened spots that may be filled with fluid or pus. Also, preceded by a descriptive word (rare or obsolete), an illness characterized by a type of rash.","example":"He came out in a rash because of an allergy.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["overrash","rashful","rashling","rashly","rashness","unrash","rashie","rashless","rashlike","rashy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rash#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d09d71af31f849fad4","definition":"An irregular distribution or sprinkling of objects resembling a rash (sense 1).","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively","wordFamily":["overrash","rashful","rashling","rashly","rashness","unrash","rashie","rashless","rashlike","rashy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rash#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:247b1db055e1a14516","definition":"An outbreak or surge in problems; a spate, string, or trend.","example":"There has been a rash of vandalism lately.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["epidemic"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively","wordFamily":["overrash","rashful","rashling","rashly","rashness","unrash","rashie","rashless","rashlike","rashy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rash#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0a0f19efbda4ef8127","definition":"Chiefly preceded by a descriptive word: a fabric with a smooth texture woven from silk, worsted, or a mixture of the two, intended as an inferior substitute for silk.","example":"cloth rash    silk rash","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"historical","register":"historical, uncountable","wordFamily":["overrash","rashful","rashling","rashly","rashness","unrash","rashie","rashless","rashlike","rashy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rash#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4f5f591dbef3af7ee1","definition":"A soft crackling or rustling sound.","example":"Look on thoſe grave plodding fellovvs, […] I'll undertake three parts of four are going to their Courtezans. I tell thee, Jack, the vvhiſking of a Silk-Govvn, and the raſh of a Tabby-Pettycoat, are as comfortable ſounds to one of theſe rich Citizens, as the chink of their Pieces of Eight.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["overrash","rashful","rashling","rashly","rashness","unrash","rashie","rashless","rashlike","rashy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rash#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b81bb26c4885955f17","definition":"To forcefully move or push (someone or something) in a certain direction.","example":"Reg[an]. VVherefore to Douer ſir? / Gloſt[er, i.e., Gloucester]. Becauſe I vvould not ſee thy cruell nayles / Pluck out his poore old eyes, nor thy fierce ſiſter / In his aurynted fleſh raſh boriſh phangs, […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Scotland, archaic, obsolete","register":"Scotland, archaic, obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["overrash","rashful","rashling","rashly","rashness","unrash","rashie","rashless","rashlike","rashy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rash#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0d0b80ae8d74e315b0","definition":"To break (something) forcefully; to smash.","example":"Fair lordes sayd syre Launcelot leue your noyse and your rassyng and I shalle sette open this dore and thenne may ye doo with me what it lyketh yow.\n\"Fair lords, said Sir Launcelot, leave your noise and your rashing, and I shall set open this door, and then may ye do with me what it liketh you.\"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Scotland, archaic, obsolete","register":"Scotland, archaic, obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["overrash","rashful","rashling","rashly","rashness","unrash","rashie","rashless","rashlike","rashy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rash#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:812efab131fdcafecf","definition":"To emit or issue (something) hastily.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Scotland, archaic, obsolete","register":"Scotland, archaic, obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["overrash","rashful","rashling","rashly","rashness","unrash","rashie","rashless","rashlike","rashy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rash#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ed17759bbc22a1f711","definition":"Usually followed by up: to prepare (something) with haste; to cobble together, to improvise.","example":"Retur[n]e to the places of Peter, the one in his firſt epiſtle, the other in the latter: and ſo be you contented with this preſent anſvver raſhed up in haſte.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Scotland, archaic, obsolete, rare","register":"Scotland, archaic, obsolete, rare, transitive","wordFamily":["overrash","rashful","rashling","rashly","rashness","unrash","rashie","rashless","rashlike","rashy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rash#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ed4bc384ca581937c8","definition":"To move forcefully, hastily, or suddenly; to dash, to rush.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Scotland, archaic, obsolete","register":"Scotland, archaic, intransitive, obsolete","wordFamily":["overrash","rashful","rashling","rashly","rashness","unrash","rashie","rashless","rashlike","rashy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rash#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:cb0b9077e143f5e039","definition":"To fall heavily; to dash down.","example":"[…] the rain rashed down - the road was battered, As with the force of billows shattered; […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Scotland, archaic, obsolete","register":"Scotland, archaic, intransitive, obsolete","wordFamily":["overrash","rashful","rashling","rashly","rashness","unrash","rashie","rashless","rashlike","rashy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rash#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d9394e9035df05f4a8","definition":"Chiefly followed by against, at, or upon: To collide or hit.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Scotland, archaic, obsolete","register":"Scotland, archaic, intransitive, obsolete","wordFamily":["overrash","rashful","rashling","rashly","rashness","unrash","rashie","rashless","rashlike","rashy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rash#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:efa23d69b9ed59b71b","definition":"Chiefly followed by away, down, off, out, etc.: to pluck, pull, or rip (something) violently.","example":"There Marinell great deeds of armes did ſhevv; / And through the thickeſt like a Lyon flevv, / Raſhing off helmes, and ryuing plates a ſonder, / That euery one his daunger did eſchevv.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Scotland, archaic, obsolete","register":"Scotland, archaic, obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["overrash","rashful","rashling","rashly","rashness","unrash","rashie","rashless","rashlike","rashy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rash#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:efb90b52f8acebad65","definition":"To hack, slash, or slice (something).","exam